# decision-when-named-reduction root (#189 Slice-C boundary 1, impl-panel round 1 critical A)
library "Pol".

// A decision whose `when` guard is a NAMED, code-LESS reduction ("Enough Trials" = `count "Trial
// Records" at least 2`). The named reduction has NO own `code is`, so `collectCaseFeatures` never
// returns it — a case-feature-collection-based gate is SILENT and the decision would emit a vacuous
// empty-input / no-SD guard under success:true. The FHIR loud gate keys on the decision GUARD SURFACE
// (`interfaceConceptNames`), so it catches this form too.

concept "Trial Records":
- type is Observation.
- shape is RecordSet.
- code is `trial`.

concept "Enough Trials":
- value type is boolean.
- definition is count "Trial Records" at least 2.

decision "Cov Determination":
first:
- when "Enough Trials" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

activity "certify.Approve":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVE`.
activity "not-certify.Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `DENY`.
